#=GF DR   INTERPRO; IPR007153;
#=GF DR   SCOP; 1rlh; fa;
#=GF DR   SO; 0100021; polypeptide_conserved_region;
#=GF CC   The structure of a member of this family from the
#=GF CC   hyperthermophilic archaeon Pyrobaculum aerophilum contains a
#=GF CC   modified histidine residue which is interpreted as stable
#=GF CC   phosphorylation [1]. In vitro binding studies confirmed that
#=GF CC   adenosine and AMP but not ADP or ATP bind to the protein [1].
